        {
          "text": "In the initial phase, the subject experiences involuntary breath-holding, followed by “air hunger,” an overwhelming urge",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 207
        }
      ],
      "words": 23
    },
    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "This agitation is reflexive, driven by the brainstem. As hypoxia progresses, cognitive function deteriorates rapidly. Me",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 733
        }
      ],
      "words": 37
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "This is not relief, but neurological decline. The brain, deprived of oxygen, begins shutting down nonessential function.",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1010
        }
      ],
      "words": 23
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Cardiac arrest follows shortly thereafter. Drowning should be considered a prolonged and distressing form of asphyxiatio",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1175
